# Calibrate the focus lens by sweeping it to both mechanical limits using
# StallGuard, then establishing the normalized [0.0, 1.0] travel range.
#
# Homing is host-triggered and never runs automatically on power-up: the MCU
# cannot know whether driving the lens into a stop is safe at that moment.
# Calibration is persisted to flash, so on a normal reboot the lens comes back
# IDLE and this action is the exception rather than the rule.
#
# The firmware runs the sweep on core 1 alongside step generation; this action
# server only supervises it, so feedback tracks HomingPhase transitions rather
# than being emitted on a timer.

# Goal: empty. Homing has no parameters — the sweep velocity, StallGuard
# threshold and back-off are firmware build-time constants (config.h).

---

# True only if both limits were found and a valid calibration was committed.
bool success

# Total usable travel between the homed limits, in microsteps. Integral
# because the firmware tracks limits as int32_t step counts (README section
# 5.2 says float32; that is a documentation slip, not a wider range).
int32 range_steps

# Human-readable reason on failure; empty on success.
string<=64 message

---

# Mirrors the firmware HomingPhase enum in state.h. Note this is offset by one
# from README section 5.2, which omits PHASE_NONE and so numbers the rest
# starting at zero.
uint8 PHASE_NONE = 0
uint8 PHASE_SEEKING_MAX = 1
uint8 PHASE_SEEKING_MIN = 2
uint8 PHASE_ZEROING = 3

uint8 phase
string<=32 phase_description
